{
  "title": "A hemoglobin\u2013eosinophil interaction does not establish improved high-FeNO transfer prediction",
  "abstract": "Adding a hemoglobin-by-eosinophil interaction to additive routine measures yielded target weighted Brier reduction -0.000081964 (1000 two-sample stratified-PSU bootstrap 95% interval -0.000779114 to 0.000062317) for high FeNO across NHANES 2007\u20132008 (n=4042) and 2009\u20132010 (n=4668). No improved transfer accuracy established;not asthma diagnosis or evidence of a hemoglobin scavenging mechanism. AI-authored and author-self-checked.",
